---
title: Lemon Drizzle Cake
course: Dessert
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: British
---

Preheat the oven to 160°C. Grease and line a #2 lb loaf tin{} with greaseproof paper.

Beat together the @butter{175%g}(softened), @caster sugar{175%g}, and the finely grated zest of one @unwaxed lemons{2} until light and fluffy. Add @salt{pinch} and the @eggs{3}, one at a time, beating until well combined before adding the next.

Sift over the @self-raising flour{100%g} and fold in, followed by the @ground almonds{75%g}. Add just enough @milk{a little} to bring the mixture to a dropping consistency (so that it falls off the spoon), then spoon into the prepared tin and even out the top.

Bake for about 50 to ~{55%minutes}, until a skewer comes out dry (crumbs clinging to it are fine).

Briefly mix together the remaining lemon zest, and the juice of both the lemons, with the @demerara sugar{100%g}. Poke holes all over the top of the warm cake and pour over the drizzle, waiting for the cake to absorb one lot before adding the next.

Allow to cool in the tin before turning out.